<!--
  nuTerra light catalogue - what light a MODEL emits.

  Keyed on the .primitives path, the only identity a model has that survives
  across maps: batch and model ids are per space and there is no display name
  in the data at all. One row lights every instance on every map that has it -
  3465 copies of TownEnv_StreetLamp4 alone.

  POSITIONS ARE NOT HERE. They are in map_lights.xml, one table per map,
  regenerated by "nuTerra.exe scanlights=<path>" straight from space.bin. This
  file is the part a human tunes; that one is the part a machine rebuilds.

  columns
    name        for the UI
    kind        lamp | fire | glow, from the material FX
    primitives  the asset path, and the key
    type        point | spot | area
                  point  radiates in every direction. A bare bulb, a fire.
                  spot   a cone, aimed by yaw/pitch. A street lamp has a cowl
                         over the bulb, and a SCONCE is bolted to a wall - a
                         point light in either place shines straight back
                         through the fitting and lights the wall behind it.
                  area   a broad soft emitter with no useful centre - a lit
                         window, a glowing panel.
    yaw pitch   where a spot AIMS, degrees, in MODEL space. yaw 0 is +Z and
                turns toward +X; pitch 0 is level and -90 is straight down.
                Ignored for point.
    cone        full cone angle in degrees. 360 on a point, for readability.
    blend       0..1, how much of the cone is soft edge. 0 is a hard circle.
    color       sRGB as authored, same convention Path Studio writes
    level       0..1, the fraction of the global Light Gain this emits
    range       metres. A light with no radius lights nothing.
    bulb        metres above the model ORIGIN - not the bounding box floor,
                which differs whenever the artist did not put the origin on
                the ground. The Lamp Inspector reads this off the mesh.
    vol_fade    how fast the SCATTERING dies across the radius. High is a
                tight halo, low fills the sphere.
    vol_mix     0..1, how much this light scatters into fog.

  EVERYTHING EXCEPT name/kind/primitives IS A GUESS. Only the street lamp
  numbers have been looked at, and those came from one lamp tuned by hand on
  19_monastery. The pitch of -90 on street lamps and -20 on sconces is
  reasoning from what the fitting is, not from measuring a mesh.
-->
